# Header checks (PCRE, case-insensitive) — every cleanup service runs them,
# inbound MX mail and authenticated submission alike (master.cf).
#
# Internal routing header: only fetchmail's LMTP delivery may set it
# (delivery-rules.sieve files mail into the folder it names).  From SMTP it
# is the sender's choice of folder for their own message — Trash, or past
# the recipient's own Sieve rules.  The validate:postfix job pins this rule.
/^X-Deliver-To-Folder[[:space:]]*:/ IGNORE

# Strip privacy-leaking headers from outgoing mail
/^Received:.*with ESMTPSA/ IGNORE
/^X-Originating-IP:/ IGNORE
/^X-Mailer:/ IGNORE
/^X-Forwarded-To:/ IGNORE
/^Resent-Date:/ IGNORE
